# Environment for the notedown systemd service.
# systemd EnvironmentFile syntax: KEY=value lines, no shell expansion.
#
# The server reads its settings (listen address, sync mode and the rest) from
# server.toml in its data folder, /var/lib/notedown/notedown-data, not from
# this file. Today the server reads no variable from here; the file is the
# place for one when an admin needs it, and systemctl restart notedown applies
# a change.
#
# Do not set NOTEDOWN_DATA here. The service would use that folder, but a
# command such as `sudo -u notedown notedown cloud account add ...` never sees
# this file and keeps using /var/lib/notedown/notedown-data. Another data
# folder needs two things instead:
#   1. --data <folder> in every notedown call, the service included
#      (sudo systemctl edit notedown: an empty ExecStart= line, then
#      ExecStart=/usr/bin/notedown serve --data <folder>);
#   2. a ReadWritePaths=<folder> line in the same drop-in, because the service
#      can write only below /var/lib/notedown.
#
# The same holds for a render_dir in server.toml outside /var/lib/notedown:
# it needs a ReadWritePaths=<folder> line in a drop-in.
